  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/F902C7">Definition <span data-tag="F902C7">6.1.2.2</span>.</a>simplicial object!of an $\infty $-category Let $\cDelta _{+}$Delta+@$\cDelta _{+}$ denote the category of finite (possibly empty) linearly ordered sets. A <em>simplicial object</em> of an $\infty $-category $\calC $ is a map of $\infty $-categories </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[ U_{\bullet }: \Nerve (\cDelta )^{op} \rightarrow \calC . \]
</div>
  <p> An <em>augmented simplicial object</em>simplicial object!augmented of $\calC $ is a map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[ U_{\bullet }^{+}: \Nerve (\cDelta _{+})^{op} \rightarrow \calC . \]
</div>
  <p>We let $\calC _{\Delta }$Delta@$\calC _{\Delta }$ denote the $\infty $-category $\Fun ( \Nerve (\cDelta )^{op}, \calC )$; we will refer to $\calC _{\Delta }$ as the <em>$\infty $-category of simplicial objects of $\calC $</em>. Similarly, we will refer to $\Fun (\Nerve (\cDelta _{+})^{op}, \calC )$ as the <em>$\infty $-category of augmented simplicial objects of $\calC $</em> and we will denote it by $\calC _{\Delta _{+}}$DeltaPlus@$\calC _{\Delta _{+}}$. </p>
  <p>If $U_{\bullet }$ is an (augmented) simplicial object of $\calC $ and $n \geq 0$ ($n \geq -1$), we will write $U_{n}$ for the object $U([n]) \in \calC $. </p>
